metacircular-univalent-unison-of-cubically-receptive-stateboxes-lines-9 = cons "In hyperactivity the hash is the reference. Code lives in the store: one reader hashes what is on disk at bootstrap, and from then on the hash is the reference. The store holds every value under its hash; the names log records who pointed which name at which content, and when. That log is version control, finer than a tree of files. Local operation and networked operation are the same interaction over content-addressed values, with a handler crossing a network port when peers exchange objects (`Sig`, `ParState`, §§7.6, 10.6, 10.8); there is no canonical state and no central server owning the store. Any command-line or web view is just a projection of the same values, and publishing is pointing a name in a shared view at a content key." (cons "" nil)
